{"schema":"learning-v2-theory.v1","lesson":3,"lang":"pl","title":"Rzeczy: a, an, the, this, these","sections":[{"num":"01","title":"Czego się nauczysz","defaultOpen":true,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"W tej lekcji uczysz się nazywać rzeczy wokół siebie: «to krzesło», «to bilety», «ta ładowarka», «tamte kwiaty są świeże», «błąd jest tutaj», «to czerwony kubek». Angielski ma do tego małe słówka przed rzeczą: a, an, the, this, that."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"It is a chair.","translation":"To jest krzesło.","hi":"a"},{"en":"They are tickets.","translation":"To są bilety.","hi":"tickets"},{"en":"This is a charger.","translation":"To jest ładowarka. *(w mojej ręce)*","hi":"This"},{"en":"Those flowers are fresh.","translation":"Tamte kwiaty są świeże.","hi":"Those"},{"en":"It is a red cup.","translation":"To czerwony kubek.","hi":"red"}]}]},{"num":"02","title":"Jedna rzecz — przed nią a","defaultOpen":true,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Po polsku mówimy po prostu «To jest krzesło». Po angielsku przed jedną rzeczą prawie zawsze stoi małe a: It is a chair. a się nie tłumaczy. Pokazuje tylko, że rzecz jest jedna i właśnie ją nazywasz."},{"kind":"formula","formula":[{"text":"It is","accent":true},{"text":"a","accent":true},{"text":"rzecz","accent":true}]},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"It is a chair.","translation":"To jest krzesło.","hi":"a"},{"en":"It's a lamp.","translation":"To lampa.","hi":"a"},{"en":"Is it a table?","translation":"Czy to stół?","hi":"a"},{"en":"It is a key.","translation":"To klucz.","hi":"a"},{"en":"It is not a window.","translation":"To nie jest okno.","hi":"a"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"It is chair.","right":"It is a chair."},{"wrong":"Is it table?","right":"Is it a table?"}]},{"kind":"tip","text":"W pytaniu i w «nie» a zostaje na miejscu: Is it a table? It is not a window."}]},{"num":"03","title":"a czy an — decyduje pierwszy dźwięk","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Jeśli słowo zaczyna się od samogłoski, zamiast a mówi się an: an armchair, an oven, an umbrella. Tak łatwiej to wymówić: «a-armczea» się potyka, a «en-armczea» brzmi gładko."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"It is an armchair.","translation":"To fotel.","hi":"an"},{"en":"Is it an oven?","translation":"Czy to piekarnik?","hi":"an"},{"en":"It's an umbrella.","translation":"To parasol.","hi":"an"},{"en":"It is an earring.","translation":"To kolczyk.","hi":"an"},{"en":"It's an egg.","translation":"To jajko.","hi":"an"},{"en":"It is an invoice.","translation":"To faktura.","hi":"an"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"It is a oven.","right":"It is an oven."},{"wrong":"It's a egg.","right":"It's an egg."}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"choice","kind":"choice","before":"It's","after":"umbrella.","options":["a","an","the"],"answer":"an","why":"umbrella zaczyna się od samogłoski, więc an."}}]},{"num":"04","title":"Dźwięk, a nie litera","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Patrz na dźwięk, a nie na literę. W hour litera h się nie czyta — słowo brzmi «auer», więc an hour. A uniform i euro zaczynają się od «j» («juniform», «juro») — to nie samogłoska, więc a."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"It is an hour.","translation":"To jest godzina.","hi":"an"},{"en":"Is it a uniform?","translation":"Czy to mundur?","hi":"a"},{"en":"It's a euro.","translation":"To euro.","hi":"a"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"It is a hour.","right":"It is an hour."},{"wrong":"It's an euro.","right":"It's a euro."}]},{"kind":"tip","text":"Prosty test: powiedz słowo na głos. Zaczyna się od «a», «e», «o», «u» — an. Od «j» albo spółgłoski — a."}]},{"num":"05","title":"Wiele rzeczy: dodaj s, a a usuń","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Gdy rzeczy jest kilka, do słowa dodaje się s: ticket → tickets. A a znika, bo znaczy «jedna». Zmienia się też słowo w środku: o jednej rzeczy — it is, o kilku — they are."},{"kind":"formula","formula":[{"text":"They are","accent":true},{"text":"rzecz + s","accent":false}]},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"They are tickets.","translation":"To są bilety.","hi":"tickets"},{"en":"Are they coins?","translation":"Czy to monety?","hi":"coins"},{"en":"The cards are new.","translation":"Kartki są nowe.","hi":"cards"},{"en":"They are towels.","translation":"To są ręczniki.","hi":"towels"},{"en":"They are spoons.","translation":"To są łyżki.","hi":"spoons"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"They are a tickets.","right":"They are tickets."},{"wrong":"They are ticket.","right":"They are tickets."},{"wrong":"It is tickets.","right":"They are tickets."}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"word_bank","kind":"word_bank","prompt":"Kurier dał ci kilka biletów. Powiedz: «To są bilety».","answer":["They","are","tickets"],"slotLabels":["kto","słowo","co"],"distractors":["a","ticket"]}}]},{"num":"06","title":"Kiedy potrzebne jest es","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Jeśli słowo kończy się na s, sh albo ch, samego s nie da się wymówić. Wtedy dodaje się es i pojawia się dodatkowa sylaba: bus → buses, dish → dishes, watch → watches. Słychać ją: «basiz», «diszyz»."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"They are buses.","translation":"To są autobusy.","hi":"buses"},{"en":"Are they dishes?","translation":"Czy to talerze?","hi":"dishes"},{"en":"The watches are old.","translation":"Zegarki są stare.","hi":"watches"},{"en":"They are glasses.","translation":"To są szklanki.","hi":"glasses"},{"en":"Are they brushes?","translation":"Czy to szczotki?","hi":"brushes"},{"en":"The benches are here.","translation":"Ławki są tutaj.","hi":"benches"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"They are buss.","right":"They are buses."},{"wrong":"The watchs are old.","right":"The watches are old."}]}]},{"num":"07","title":"Kiedy y zmienia się w ies","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Jeśli słowo kończy się na y, a przed nim stoi spółgłoska, y zmienia się w ies: battery → batteries, city → cities. Brzmi prawie tak samo, tylko na końcu słychać «z»."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"They are batteries.","translation":"To są baterie.","hi":"batteries"},{"en":"Are they countries?","translation":"Czy to kraje?","hi":"countries"},{"en":"Where are the stories?","translation":"Gdzie są bajki?","hi":"stories"},{"en":"They are cities.","translation":"To są miasta.","hi":"cities"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"They are batterys.","right":"They are batteries."},{"wrong":"Where are the storys?","right":"Where are the stories?"}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"choice","kind":"choice","before":"Are they","after":"?","options":["countrys","countries","countryes"],"answer":"countries","why":"Przed y stoi spółgłoska r, więc y zmienia się w ies."}}]},{"num":"08","title":"this i that: blisko czy tam","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Po polsku to, co masz w ręce, i to, co stoi na drugim końcu sali, to po prostu «to». Po angielsku wybiera się według odległości. Blisko, w zasięgu ręki — this. Daleko, pokazujesz palcem — that."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"This is a charger.","translation":"To jest ładowarka. *(w ręce)*","hi":"This"},{"en":"This is an adapter.","translation":"To jest przejściówka. *(w ręce)*","hi":"This"},{"en":"That is a screen.","translation":"To jest ekran. *(tam)*","hi":"That"},{"en":"Is this a remote?","translation":"Czy to pilot? *(blisko)*","hi":"this"},{"en":"Is that a button?","translation":"Czy to przycisk? *(tam)*","hi":"that"},{"en":"That is not a keyring.","translation":"To nie jest brelok. *(tam)*","hi":"That"}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"binary","kind":"binary","question":"Ekran wisi na dalekiej ścianie sali. Jak powiesz?","optionA":"This is a screen.","optionB":"That is a screen.","correct":"B","explain":"Ekran jest daleko, więc that."}}]},{"num":"09","title":"these i those: kiedy rzeczy jest kilka","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Dla kilku rzeczy this zmienia się w these, a that — w those. I w środku jest are. Blisko — these are, daleko — those are."},{"kind":"formula","formula":[{"text":"jedna blisko: this is","accent":false},{"text":"kilka blisko: these are","accent":false},{"text":"jedna daleko: that is","accent":false},{"text":"kilka daleko: those are","accent":false}]},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"These are shoes.","translation":"To są buty. *(przede mną)*","hi":"These"},{"en":"Those are blankets.","translation":"To są koce. *(tam)*","hi":"Those"},{"en":"Are these socks new?","translation":"Czy te skarpetki są nowe?","hi":"these"},{"en":"Those sheets are big.","translation":"Tamte prześcieradła są duże.","hi":"Those"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"This are shoes.","right":"These are shoes."},{"wrong":"These is shoes.","right":"These are shoes."},{"wrong":"Those is blankets.","right":"Those are blankets."}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"choice","kind":"choice","before":"","after":"are shoes.","options":["This","These","Those"],"answer":"These","why":"Butów jest kilka i są blisko: these."}}]},{"num":"10","title":"«Ten album», «tamte kwiaty»","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"this, that, these, those można postawić tuż przed rzeczą: this album — «ten album», those flowers — «tamte kwiaty». Wtedy a nie jest potrzebne. Jedna rzecz — this albo that, kilka — these albo those, a słowo ma s."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"This album is big.","translation":"Ten album jest duży.","hi":"This"},{"en":"These frames are cheap.","translation":"Te ramki są tanie.","hi":"These"},{"en":"Those flowers are fresh.","translation":"Tamte kwiaty są świeże.","hi":"Those"},{"en":"This building is new.","translation":"Ten budynek jest nowy.","hi":"This"},{"en":"Is this lemon ripe?","translation":"Czy ta cytryna jest dojrzała?","hi":"this"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"This a album is big.","right":"This album is big."},{"wrong":"These frame are cheap.","right":"These frames are cheap."},{"wrong":"This frames are cheap.","right":"These frames are cheap."}]}]},{"num":"11","title":"a czy the","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"a — kiedy nazywasz rzecz albo osobę pierwszy raz i rozmówca jeszcze nie wie, o kogo chodzi: A cashier is here. the — kiedy oboje wiecie, o czym mowa: widzicie to, jest tylko jedno albo już o tym było. The mistake is here."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"A cashier is here.","translation":"Jest tu kasjer.","hi":"A"},{"en":"This is a receipt.","translation":"To jest paragon.","hi":"a"},{"en":"The mistake is here.","translation":"Błąd jest tutaj. *(ten, o którym mówiliśmy)*","hi":"The"},{"en":"The handle is broken.","translation":"Klamka jest zepsuta. *(w tych drzwiach)*","hi":"The"},{"en":"The seller is busy.","translation":"Sprzedawca jest zajęty. *(ten tutaj)*","hi":"The"},{"en":"An item is missing.","translation":"Brakuje jednego produktu.","hi":"An"}]},{"kind":"tip","text":"Najpierw a, potem the: This is a mistake. — Gdzie? — The mistake is here. Rzecz już padła, teraz oboje wiecie, o którą chodzi."},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"choice","kind":"choice","before":"","after":"mistake is here.","options":["A","An","The"],"answer":"The","why":"Oboje wiecie, o który błąd chodzi, więc the."}}]},{"num":"12","title":"O rzeczach w ogóle — bez a i bez the","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Kiedy mówisz nie o konkretnych rzeczach, tylko o takich rzeczach w ogóle, wystarczy słowo z s: Books are heavy — «książki są ciężkie» (jakiekolwiek). The magazines are new — to już konkretne czasopisma, które oboje widzicie."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"Books are heavy.","translation":"Książki są ciężkie. *(w ogóle)*","hi":"Books"},{"en":"Newspapers are cheap.","translation":"Gazety są tanie. *(w ogóle)*","hi":"Newspapers"},{"en":"Wrenches are expensive.","translation":"Klucze płaskie są drogie. *(w ogóle)*","hi":"Wrenches"},{"en":"The magazines are new.","translation":"Czasopisma są nowe. *(te tutaj)*","hi":"The"},{"en":"The stairs are narrow.","translation":"Schody są wąskie. *(w tym budynku)*","hi":"The"}]}]},{"num":"13","title":"Kolor i cecha — przed rzeczą, bez końcówek","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Po polsku «czerwony kubek», i po angielsku ta sama kolejność: najpierw cecha, potem rzecz — a red cup. Ale kolor się nie odmienia: black chairs, a nie blacks chairs. a czy an wybierasz po pierwszym dźwięku słowa zaraz po nim: an olive coat."},{"kind":"formula","formula":[{"text":"a / an / this / these","accent":true},{"text":"kolor albo cecha","accent":true},{"text":"rzecz","accent":true}]},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"It is a red cup.","translation":"To czerwony kubek.","hi":"red"},{"en":"It is an olive coat.","translation":"To płaszcz w kolorze oliwkowym.","hi":"an"},{"en":"These are black chairs.","translation":"To są czarne krzesła.","hi":"black"},{"en":"This round table is heavy.","translation":"Ten okrągły stół jest ciężki.","hi":"round"},{"en":"These metal boxes are heavy.","translation":"Te metalowe pudełka są ciężkie.","hi":"metal"},{"en":"This striped scarf is new.","translation":"Ten szalik w paski jest nowy.","hi":"striped"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"These are blacks chairs.","right":"These are black chairs."},{"wrong":"It is a olive coat.","right":"It is an olive coat."},{"wrong":"It is a cup red.","right":"It is a red cup."}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"word_bank","kind":"word_bank","prompt":"Sprzedawca pyta, który kubek chcesz. Powiedz: «To czerwony kubek».","answer":["It","is","a","red","cup"],"slotLabels":["kto","słowo","jeden","jaki","co"],"distractors":["an","reds"]}}]},{"num":"14","title":"Błędy, które robi prawie każdy","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"It is chair.","right":"It is a chair."},{"wrong":"It is a oven.","right":"It is an oven."},{"wrong":"It is a hour.","right":"It is an hour."},{"wrong":"They are a tickets.","right":"They are tickets."},{"wrong":"They are batterys.","right":"They are batteries."},{"wrong":"This are shoes.","right":"These are shoes."},{"wrong":"These are blacks chairs.","right":"These are black chairs."}]},{"kind":"tip","text":"Zanim nazwiesz rzecz, zadaj sobie dwa pytania. Jedna czy kilka? Jedna — a/an, this/that. Kilka — s na końcu, these/those, are. I drugie: czy rozmówca wie, o którą chodzi? Jeśli tak — the."},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"binary","kind":"binary","question":"Koszule leżą przed tobą. Które zdanie jest poprawne?","optionA":"This shirts are clean.","optionB":"These shirts are clean.","correct":"B","explain":"Koszul jest kilka i są blisko: these."}}]},{"num":"15","title":"Co zabrać do ćwiczeń","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Jedna rzecz — a albo an po pierwszym dźwięku. Kilka — s, bez a. Blisko — this / these, daleko — that / those. Rzecz, którą oboje znacie, — the. Kolor i cecha przed rzeczą i bez końcówek: a red cup."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"It is an hour.","translation":"To jest godzina.","hi":"an"},{"en":"They are batteries.","translation":"To są baterie.","hi":"batteries"},{"en":"Those flowers are fresh.","translation":"Tamte kwiaty są świeże.","hi":"Those"},{"en":"The mistake is here.","translation":"Błąd jest tutaj.","hi":"The"},{"en":"It is a red cup.","translation":"To czerwony kubek.","hi":"red"}]}]}],"sessionSection":{"1":"02","2":"02","3":"02","4":"02","5":"02","6":"02","7":"02","8":"02","9":"03","10":"03","11":"04","12":"04","13":"04","14":"04","15":"04","16":"04","17":"05","18":"06","19":"07","20":"07","21":"07","22":"07","23":"07","24":"07","25":"08","26":"08","27":"08","28":"08","29":"08","30":"08","31":"08","32":"08","33":"09","34":"09","35":"10","36":"10","37":"10","38":"10","39":"10","40":"10","41":"11","42":"11","43":"12","44":"12","45":"12","46":"12","47":"12","48":"12","49":"13","50":"13","51":"13","52":"13","53":"13","54":"13","55":"13","56":"13"}}
